{
  "name": "Molding Installation: A Professional's Process",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When you're looking at getting new molding installed, you want it done right, and there's a specific process professionals follow to achieve that seamless look. First up, it's all about choosing the right profile for your room – what style and size will best complement your space? Once that's decided, careful measurement is absolutely critical. This isn't just a quick tape measure job; it involves understanding the nuances of your walls and making allowances for any unevenness. Then come the test miter cuts. This step is super important for getting those corners just right, especially in rooms where walls might not be perfectly square. After the cuts are perfected, the molding is installed. This part needs a steady hand and attention to detail to ensure each piece fits snugly and securely. Finally, to achieve that truly finished look, any small gaps are carefully caulked or filled, and sometimes a light sand is needed before painting or staining. This meticulous approach ensures that your molding looks like it was always meant to be there, adding elegance and value to your home. The more profiles, corners, or custom details involved, the more coordination and labor the job requires, which is why a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can make all the difference in delivering a flawless result.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
